    "max_awards": null,
    "plot": "Detective Jack Steele arrives at the Greasy Spoon diner on a rainy night after his informant, Toothpick Charlie, missed their scheduled drop. The diner is a laundering front for Don Moretti's syndicate. Charlie snooped too close to the books and was locked inside the sub-zero walk-in freezer by the night manager, Vinny. Because direct violence will blow Steele's cover and bring the whole syndicate down on him, Steele must work the room using wit, diner slang, and detective work. He must navigate the suspicious staff, decode hidden combinations scattered through the diner, heat up the basement boiler to distract the muscle, crack the manager's safe for the mob ledger, and unlock the walk-in freezer before Charlie becomes a permanent popsicle.",
    "rules": "Combat is disabled in this undercover investigation. Rely on observation, reading clues, learning diner slang, manipulating mechanisms, and unlocking containers and doors. Pay close attention to decorative details in rooms when solving counting riddles.\n\nIn the walk-in freezer, taking possession of the secret memo includes immediately freeing Charlie and getting him safely out of the cold. If Steele already carries the memo when he enters, the rescue happens on arrival instead. Resolve this rescue and set charlie_rescued to true before announcing Chapter 3's completion. Reading the memo reveals its information; it is not required to perform the rescue, regardless of any chapter walkthrough wording that suggests otherwise.",
    "intro_text": "Cold rain drums against the flickering neon sign of the Greasy Spoon Diner, casting bloody red reflections across the wet vestibule tiles. You adjust your collar and check the ##MATCHBOOK in your pocket. Toothpick Charlie was supposed to meet you an hour ago with the Moretti family's payoff schedule, but his booth is empty and his trail stops right at this front door.\n\nThrough the steamed-up glass separating the vestibule from the main dining room, you smell burnt coffee, fry oil, and cheap cologne. If you start flashing a badge or throwing punches, Vinny's goons will make sure neither you nor Charlie ever see morning. You'll have to play it smart, blend in, and pry this place open from the inside.",
    "completed_condition": "",
    "gameover_condition": "",
    "completed_guard_expression": "tw.vars.get('charlie_rescued') == True and tw.player.has_item('MOB_LEDGER')",
    "gameover_guard_expression": "tw.player.hp <= 0 or tw.vars.get('cover_blown') == True",
